   $q$Which sentence about the weather station uses commas correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rooftop weather station measures several conditions: such as humidity, wind speed, and air pressure.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-before-such-as"},{"text":"The rooftop weather station measures several conditions, such as: humidity, wind speed, and air pressure.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-such-as"},{"text":"The rooftop weather station measures several conditions, such as humidity, wind speed, and air pressure.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The rooftop weather station measures several conditions such as; humidity, wind speed, and air pressure.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-list"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The rooftop weather station measures several conditions, such as humidity, wind speed, and air pressure.$q$, $q$"Such as" already introduces the examples, so no colon is needed after it. A colon placed right after "such as" interrupts the phrase before its objects.$q$, 'draft', null)
