   $q$Which sentence correctly uses a prefix with a proper noun?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The cross-country team's regional meet was moved to midSeptember.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-hyphen-with-prefix"},{"text":"The cross-country team's regional meet was moved to mid-September.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The cross-country team's regional meet was moved to Mid-September.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"prefix-capitalized"},{"text":"The cross-country team's regional meet was moved to mid-september.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"proper-noun-lowercase"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The cross-country team's regional meet was moved to mid-September.$q$, $q$When a prefix such as "mid" comes before a capitalized word, a hyphen separates them and the proper noun keeps its capital: "mid-September." The prefix itself stays lowercase because it is not part of the month's name.$q$, 'draft', null)
