   $q$Which sentence correctly punctuates and capitalizes the short story title?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Our class discussed the short story \"The Salt road,\" which a local author wrote last year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"title-word-lowercase"},{"text":"Our class discussed the short story \"the Salt Road,\" which a local author wrote last year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"title-first-word-lowercase"},{"text":"Our class discussed the short story \"The Salt Road,\" which a local author wrote last year.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Our class discussed the short story \"The Salt Road\", which a local author wrote last year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-outside-quotes"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Our class discussed the short story "The Salt Road," which a local author wrote last year.$q$, $q$In American usage, a comma that follows a quoted title goes inside the closing quotation mark, and every important word in the title is capitalized. Placing the comma outside the quotation marks follows a different convention than the one used in American English.$q$, 'draft', null)
