   $q$Lucia is writing the title of a research paper about traditional boat building. Which title is capitalized correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The Art Of Building A Canoe","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"minor-words-capitalized"},{"text":"The Art of Building a Canoe","is_correct":true},{"text":"The art of building a canoe","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"major-words-lowercase"},{"text":"the Art of Building a Canoe","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"first-word-lowercase"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The Art of Building a Canoe$q$, $q$In a title, the first word and all major words are capitalized, while short articles and prepositions such as "a" and "of" stay lowercase. Capitalizing "Of" and "A" treats minor words as if they were major ones.$q$, 'draft', null)
