   $q$Read the sentence: "The updated forecast changed the plan the climbers would start at dawn instead of noon." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The updated forecast changed the plan: the climbers would start at dawn instead of noon.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The updated forecast, changed the plan; the climbers would start at dawn instead of noon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-subject-verb"},{"text":"The updated forecast changed: the plan the climbers would start at dawn instead of noon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-verb"},{"text":"The updated forecast changed the plan, the climbers would start at dawn instead of noon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The updated forecast changed the plan: the climbers would start at dawn instead of noon.$q$, $q$The second clause explains how the plan changed, so a colon after the first complete clause is correct. A comma alone between the two independent clauses is a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
