   $q$Which sentence correctly punctuates the adjectives before the noun?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The hikers followed a long winding, trail up the side of the bluff.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-noun"},{"text":"The hikers followed a long, winding trail up the side of the bluff.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The hikers followed a long, winding, trail up the side of the bluff.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-noun"},{"text":"The hikers followed a, long winding trail up the side of the bluff.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-article"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The hikers followed a long, winding trail up the side of the bluff.$q$, $q$"Long" and "winding" are coordinate adjectives, since they could be reversed or joined by "and," so a comma separates them. No comma ever comes between the last adjective and the noun it describes.$q$, 'draft', null)
