   $q$How does sentence 16 control the pacing of the narrative at that moment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It uses dialogue to reveal how the narrator feels about the teacher's advice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-dialogue-present"},{"text":"It shifts the point of view so the reader sees the darkroom through Mr. Halvorsen's eyes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-pov-shift"},{"text":"It lists details in the order they appear, so the reader watches the image emerge along with the narrator.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It skips ahead in time so the reader does not have to wait through the slow chemical process.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pacing-speed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It lists details in the order they appear, so the reader watches the image emerge along with the narrator.$q$, $q$The colon and the sequence "first... then... then" slow the moment so the photograph appears piece by piece. The sentence does not skip time; it stretches a few seconds out.$q$, 'draft', '207157b6-db87-503d-969e-5fb11981642e')
