  ('76621d7b-4fb3-5831-9306-33bfa789fb0c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The writer wants sentence 8 to slow down and show the suspense of waiting. Which revision does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"We parked below the ridge and ate in silence, each of us refreshing the tracker and pretending not to.","is_correct":true},{"text":"We drove toward the last location, which was about nineteen miles north of the school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-fact-not-suspense"},{"text":"We drove, ate, and waited, and then the box was found and everything turned out fine.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"rushes-resolution"},{"text":"We drove toward the last location, ate our lunch quickly, and then waited for a pretty long time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-not-vivid"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$We parked below the ridge and ate in silence, each of us refreshing the tracker and pretending not to.$q$, $q$The silence and the secret refreshing show the group's anxiety through action, stretching the wait. The "pretty long time" choice tells the reader time passed but gives nothing to see or feel.$q$, 'draft', '323f5b14-65ea-5553-9c2c-4a53693e5ffc')
