   $q$After sentence 16 is removed, which sentence would make the strongest conclusion for the narrative?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Staring at that black sky, I understood that something we built from foam and tape had gone farther than any of us ever would.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Weather balloons help scientists learn about the upper atmosphere, which makes them very useful tools.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Ruth Lindqvist told us she would watch for our balloon again next year if we decided to launch another one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ends-on-minor-thread"},{"text":"The next day we wrote a lab report about the temperature data and turned it in to Ms. Adeyemi-Clarke.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Staring at that black sky, I understood that something we built from foam and tape had gone farther than any of us ever would.$q$, $q$The correct choice reflects on the meaning of the footage and connects back to the homemade box in sentence 1. The lab report choice reports the next step but never says what the experience meant.$q$, 'draft', '323f5b14-65ea-5553-9c2c-4a53693e5ffc')
