   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 16 as a conclusion that reflects on what the narrator experienced?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Then we rowed back to the dock, lifted the Heron out of the water, and put it back on its rack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"},{"text":"Rowing is one of the oldest sports in the world and is popular at many high schools and colleges.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Carrying the Heron back to its rack, I realized I had spent two weeks fixing my rowing alone when the answer sat right in front of me.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Everyone on the team was extremely happy, and we all agreed that it had been a really great race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tells-emotion-vaguely"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Carrying the Heron back to its rack, I realized I had spent two weeks fixing my rowing alone when the answer sat right in front of me.$q$, $q$The correct choice reflects on the lesson of the race, linking back to the narrator's private struggle in sentences 5 through 7 and the solution in sentence 12. The "extremely happy" choice only restates sentence 16 with more words.$q$, 'draft', '2467747a-cf2a-53b6-97a6-bd364b396dca')
