   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 16 as a conclusion that reflects on the experience?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I helped Dr. Siddiqui tag monarch butterflies in a meadow behind the county nature center.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-situation"},{"text":"Monarch butterflies are orange and black, and many of them migrate south every single autumn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Weeks later I still thought about that monarch, and about how catching it had depended on my learning to stand still.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Then Dr. Siddiqui and I packed up the nets and the tags and walked back to the nature center.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Weeks later I still thought about that monarch, and about how catching it had depended on my learning to stand still.$q$, $q$The correct choice reflects on the lesson of patience that runs from sentence 7 to the catch. The choice about packing up ends with action but no meaning.$q$, 'draft', 'ce1c39f0-3b8d-5408-9e55-8e95fc81e268')
