   $q$Why does the writer use three short sentences, sentences 13 through 15, for the release?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To summarize the entire migration of the monarch to its winter home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-scope"},{"text":"To hurry past the release so the story can quickly reach its conclusion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pacing-speed"},{"text":"To show that the narrator is confused and unsure what to do next.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To break the release into separate beats so the reader lingers on each moment of the departure.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To break the release into separate beats so the reader lingers on each moment of the departure.$q$, $q$Each sentence holds one beat (opening the hand, the pause, the flight), which slows the moment rather than rushing it. Nothing in the text suggests confusion; the narrator acts calmly after being shown what to do.$q$, 'draft', 'ce1c39f0-3b8d-5408-9e55-8e95fc81e268')
