-- Passage wg11-narrative-writing-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('0263af8c-9911-59cf-b483-df6aaced16f9', 'wg11-narrative-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Last Shovel$q$, $q$(1) My first week working at Pell's Hardware happened to be the week of the biggest snowstorm in a decade. (2) By Thursday afternoon, the parking lot had become a gray sea of slush, and the line at the register stretched past the paint aisle. (3) Mr. Pell, who had owned the store for thirty years, moved between the aisles with a clipboard, calmly telling customers what was left. (4) I was running the register by myself for the first time.

(5) At four o'clock, we sold our last bag of rock salt. (6) At four-fifteen, we sold our last snow shovel to a man who needed it for his mother's driveway. (7) Then a boy about my age came in, stamping snow off his boots, and asked whether we had any shovels left. (8) I told him no.

(9) He did not leave. (10) He explained that his family had just moved from a city where it almost never snowed, and they did not own a single winter tool. (11) His name was Emeka, and he looked as if the storm had personally insulted him.

(12) I glanced toward the back room, where I knew a dented shovel with a cracked handle sat waiting to be returned to the supplier. (13) I found Mr. Pell and asked whether we could sell it. (14) He thought for a moment, wrapped tape around the crack, and handed it to me. (15) "No charge," he said. (16) "Tell him to come back in spring for a real one."

(17) Emeka came back in April. (18) He bought a rake.$q$, 'draft')
