   $q$Read the paragraph: "____ Backdrops are painted with lines that converge toward a distant point, suggesting a long avenue. Doorways at the rear of the set are built noticeably smaller than those near the audience. Even the floor may slope gently upward toward the back wall." Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Stage designers often use forced perspective to make a shallow stage appear much deeper than it really is.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many theater backdrops are painted on large sheets of heavy canvas.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Theater has a long and varied history in many cultures around the world.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"Actors must learn their lines and blocking well before opening night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Stage designers often use forced perspective to make a shallow stage appear much deeper than it really is.$q$, $q$All three supporting sentences describe tricks that create an illusion of depth, which the forced perspective sentence names. The canvas sentence is too narrow, since it fits only the backdrops and says nothing about depth.$q$, 'draft', null)
