   $q$Read: "The new express bus line cut commute times sharply for residents of the east side. ____, ridership on the older local route that runs alongside it fell steeply, as many passengers switched to the faster option." Which transition best completes the sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In other words,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"effect-read-as-restatement"},{"text":"Likewise,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"effect-read-as-comparison"},{"text":"Nevertheless,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"effect-read-as-contrast"},{"text":"Consequently,","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Consequently,$q$, $q$Riders left the old route because the new line was faster, so the second sentence is a result of the first and "Consequently" fits. "Likewise" is tempting because both sentences describe a decrease, but the drop in ridership is caused by the new line, not parallel to it.$q$, 'draft', null)
