   $q$A student's essay has one paragraph explaining how coral bleaching occurs and a second paragraph describing projects that help damaged reefs regrow. Which sentence would best open the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bleaching happens when stressed corals expel the tiny algae that live in their tissues.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-previous-paragraph"},{"text":"Although bleaching can devastate a reef within weeks, scientists and volunteer divers are now testing ways to help damaged reefs recover.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coral reefs are found in warm, shallow waters in many parts of the world.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-no-link"},{"text":"Therefore, restoration projects have now completely solved the problem of coral bleaching.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Although bleaching can devastate a reef within weeks, scientists and volunteer divers are now testing ways to help damaged reefs recover.$q$, $q$The correct sentence refers back to bleaching (the first paragraph) and forward to recovery efforts (the second), creating a clear link. The sentence about corals expelling algae only repeats the first paragraph and does not introduce restoration.$q$, 'draft', null)
