   $q$A paragraph argues that towns should reduce unnecessary outdoor lighting. It explains that excess light hides the stars, confuses migrating birds, and wastes electricity. Which sentence best concludes the paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Streetlights also help drivers see pedestrians and reduce accidents at busy crossings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-counterpoint-at-end"},{"text":"By shielding fixtures and dimming lights late at night, a town could recover its view of the sky, protect wildlife, and lower its energy bills at the same time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Migrating birds sometimes circle brightly lit buildings for hours until they are exhausted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Many cities are also working to plant more trees along their streets and parks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By shielding fixtures and dimming lights late at night, a town could recover its view of the sky, protect wildlife, and lower its energy bills at the same time.$q$, $q$The correct sentence proposes a solution and gathers all three of the paragraph's reasons, stars, birds, and energy, into one closing statement. The sentence about birds circling buildings supports only one reason, so it works as a detail rather than a conclusion.$q$, 'draft', null)
