   $q$Read the sentences: "Marisol restored the old printing press. The press had been stored in a barn for forty years. It now prints posters for the school play." Which choice combines them most effectively?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Marisol restored the old printing press, and it had been stored in a barn for forty years, and it now prints posters for the school play.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"excessive-coordination"},{"text":"Stored in a barn for forty years, Marisol restored the old printing press, which now prints posters for the school play.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier"},{"text":"Marisol restored the old printing press, which had been stored in a barn for forty years and now prints posters for the school play.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Marisol restored the old printing press, it had been stored in a barn for forty years, it now prints posters for the school play.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Marisol restored the old printing press, which had been stored in a barn for forty years and now prints posters for the school play.$q$, $q$The relative clause "which had been stored... and now prints..." attaches both facts to the press in one clear sentence. Opening with "Stored in a barn" makes it sound as if Marisol had been stored in the barn.$q$, 'draft', null)
