  ('1649eeb6-db36-56a5-8089-227cc5453645', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-sentence-structure'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentences: "The Silk Road is often imagined as a single highway. It was actually a shifting network of routes." Which choice combines them most effectively?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Although the Silk Road is often imagined as a single highway, it was actually a shifting network of routes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Because the Silk Road is often imagined as a single highway, it was actually a shifting network of routes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"illogical-subordinator"},{"text":"The Silk Road is often imagined as a single highway, so it was actually a shifting network of routes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"illogical-coordinator"},{"text":"The Silk Road is often imagined as a single highway, it was actually a shifting network of routes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Although the Silk Road is often imagined as a single highway, it was actually a shifting network of routes.$q$, $q$The word "actually" signals a contrast between how the route is imagined and what it was, so "Although" fits. "Because" is grammatical but wrongly claims that the way people imagine the route caused its real shape.$q$, 'draft', null)
