  ('9c496dc7-237f-51be-af84-6147d666e2d1', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-sentence-structure'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "By adding a second rehearsal each week is how the choir improved its sound." Which revision fixes the mixed construction?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By adding a second rehearsal each week is the reason the choir improved its sound.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-construction-reworded"},{"text":"By adding a second rehearsal each week, the choir's sound was how it improved.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mixed-construction-unfixed"},{"text":"By adding a second rehearsal each week, the choir improved its sound.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Adding a second rehearsal each week is how the choir improved its sound, it worked.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By adding a second rehearsal each week, the choir improved its sound.$q$, $q$A prepositional phrase beginning with "By" cannot be the subject of "is," so the fix makes "the choir" the subject of "improved." The "is the reason" version keeps the same problem of a phrase acting as a subject.$q$, 'draft', null)
