   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 so that the draft states a clear claim its evidence supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Solberg's article is mostly about lichens and the trees they grow on in one coastal city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Lichens are made of a fungus and an alga living together as a single organism.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Solberg's survey shows that leafy lichens act as a living record of air quality because they react directly to pollution.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Every city should plant more oak trees so that lichens have more places to grow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Solberg's survey shows that leafy lichens act as a living record of air quality because they react directly to pollution.$q$, $q$Sentences 3 through 9 all explain how lichens respond to pollution, so a claim about lichens recording air quality fits the evidence. The choice about the article's subject only names a topic and makes no point the evidence could prove.$q$, 'draft', '27392148-b5b7-5528-9db6-194b6a6c773f')
