  ('2bf662ce-d284-5de2-a040-d0410815733e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which revision of sentence 10 best integrates the quotation into the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A quotation: \"I learned to read the toll book myself, and no clerk could cheat me after that.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dropped-quotation"},{"text":"Adjei quotes a letter from a former student who explained the lessons' value: \"I learned to read the toll book myself, and no clerk could cheat me after that.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"Adjei says that \"I learned to read the toll book myself, and no clerk could cheat me after that.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misattributed-quotation"},{"text":"\"I learned to read the toll book myself, and no clerk could cheat me after that,\" this shows the school was useful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Adjei quotes a letter from a former student who explained the lessons' value: "I learned to read the toll book myself, and no clerk could cheat me after that."$q$, $q$The revision that credits a letter from a former student names the speaker and sets up the quotation with a complete sentence and a colon. Writing "Adjei says that" wrongly makes it sound as if Adjei learned to read the toll book.$q$, 'draft', '61903b11-9d54-544c-a03c-0167e95daf4a')
