  ('99af0c4f-e30c-505e-a6a5-13b2318d3084', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence would best fill the blank in sentence 11 by explaining how the quotation supports the claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Adjei's essay also includes several other letters written by students of the school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"},{"text":"Toll books listed the charges that boats paid each time they passed through a lock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-analysis"},{"text":"The student was clearly the smartest person who ever attended the school at Lock Nine.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The student valued reading because it protected the student's pay, which shows that the school taught skills tied directly to canal work.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The student valued reading because it protected the student's pay, which shows that the school taught skills tied directly to canal work.$q$, $q$The quotation shows a worker using reading to guard those earnings, so the choice about reading protecting the student's pay connects it to the claim about lessons built around canal life. Defining a toll book only adds information and never explains why the quotation matters.$q$, 'draft', '61903b11-9d54-544c-a03c-0167e95daf4a')
