  ('451ebefe-10bc-5a0d-b3bd-a9969f981eae', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Sentence 7 shows that enrollment grew, but by itself it does not prove the claim in sentence 2. Which revision would make this evidence support the claim most effectively?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Add the exact enrollment for every winter from 1846 to 1871 so the growth is shown in full detail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"more-data-not-analysis"},{"text":"Move sentence 7 to the start of the draft so the reader sees the enrollment numbers first.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reorder-not-explain"},{"text":"Add a sentence explaining how the winter schedule and practical lessons drew those new students to the school.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Replace sentence 7 with a description of the classroom and the desks the students used.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Add a sentence explaining how the winter schedule and practical lessons drew those new students to the school.$q$, $q$Growth shows the school was popular but not why, so the writer must connect the numbers to the schedule and lessons named in the claim. Adding more yearly numbers gives more data without explaining the cause.$q$, 'draft', '61903b11-9d54-544c-a03c-0167e95daf4a')
