values
  ('f860ac4c-4c87-57d5-bb7d-1f22764099d9', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The writer wants to add a claim after sentence 1. Which sentence states the claim the draft best supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Osei shows that working with family members is always harder than working with strangers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Osei should have explained why Marisol's grandfather's hands became too stiff to steer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"},{"text":"Osei's story takes place on a ferry that carries passengers to a town called Calloway.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Osei uses the ferry bell to show Marisol growing from a reluctant helper into someone who takes responsibility for others.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Osei uses the ferry bell to show Marisol growing from a reluctant helper into someone who takes responsibility for others.$q$, $q$Both paragraphs track how Marisol rings the bell, first carelessly and then carefully, so a claim about the bell showing her growth fits. The setting choice only names where the story happens and makes no arguable point.$q$, 'draft', '57329ddd-a95d-5346-b2ef-98b651da1a8b')
