   $q$Why is sentence 8 the weakest evidence in the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It contradicts the ridership numbers reported in sentence 7.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-text"},{"text":"It comes from Haddad's own survey, so it cannot be trusted at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismisses-source"},{"text":"It is a direct quotation, and quotations should never appear in a research response.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"It is one rider's general praise and does not show how the screens changed waiting or ridership.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is one rider's general praise and does not show how the screens changed waiting or ridership.$q$, $q$A single enthusiastic opinion is not sufficient evidence for a claim about how screens raise ridership across 140 stops. The quotation does not contradict sentence 7; it simply adds little.$q$, 'draft', '552c5a16-ea51-552f-9486-690415890400')
