  ('55136006-444e-544f-8d5f-ea8a3691da5c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad's study shows that Brennick should spend its money on new buses instead of screens.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Haddad's study proves that arrival-time screens will raise ridership in every city that installs them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Haddad's study suggests that screens raised ridership by changing how waits felt, though busier stops may explain some of the gain.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Weekday boardings rose 11 percent at stops with screens and 2 percent at stops without them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad's study suggests that screens raised ridership by changing how waits felt, though busier stops may explain some of the gain.$q$, $q$The choice about screens changing how waits felt restates the claim and keeps the limitation from sentence 10, so it matches what the evidence can support. Claiming the result holds in every city stretches one study far beyond its data.$q$, 'draft', '552c5a16-ea51-552f-9486-690415890400')
