   $q$Which revision of sentence 4 best uses the writer's other sources to support the point it makes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Abebe's survey found that the average return rate for new rowers across twenty clubs is 46 percent.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-evidence"},{"text":"Leaupepe's report also says, once again, that new rowers stay because the club lets them choose morning or evening practices.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-single-source"},{"text":"Abebe's survey backs up Leaupepe's point about schedules, since clubs with flexible practice times kept more new rowers than clubs with one fixed time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Most rowers probably prefer evening practices because they are tired early in the morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Abebe's survey backs up Leaupepe's point about schedules, since clubs with flexible practice times kept more new rowers than clubs with one fixed time.$q$, $q$The choice citing Abebe's survey on flexible practice times pairs Leaupepe's claim with independent evidence from sentence 8 that addresses the same point, schedules. The 46 percent figure is from another source but does not speak to practice times.$q$, 'draft', 'fcd2195f-c892-56b6-86ef-ca3a8f145083')
