-- Passage wg11-writing-with-evidence-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('86a82509-8375-5c02-b9c8-606fc16ffac7', 'wg11-writing-with-evidence-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Patience in "Kiln Morning"$q$, $q$(1) In Nadia Ferreira-Hale's poem "Kiln Morning," a potter sits beside her studio window through the night, waiting for her kiln to cool so she can see whether her bowls survived the firing. (2) The poem is about pottery and waiting.

(3) Each of the first three stanzas ends with the line "Not yet, not yet," which the speaker repeats every time she reaches for the kiln door. (4) The repetition slows the poem down and makes the reader wait along with the speaker, feeling each small delay just as she does. (5) In the second stanza, the speaker admits that "the fire decides what my hands began," suggesting that she cannot control the final result. (6) Pottery kilns can reach temperatures of more than two thousand degrees.

(7) ____, the final stanza drops the refrain entirely. (8) When the speaker at last opens the door, she finds one cracked bowl among the rest and writes, "Even this one rang when I tapped it." (9) The speaker likes the cracked bowl.

(10) Ferreira-Hale's poem suggests that patience is not only waiting but also accepting whatever the waiting brings.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
