  ('bc1a723d-b53d-5de7-945f-f970fda3034f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which revision of sentence 2 best states a claim the rest of the draft supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ferreira-Hale's poem describes a potter, a kiln, a night of waiting and a set of bowls in four stanzas.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-claim"},{"text":"Ferreira-Hale's poem is beautiful and is one of the best poems written about making art.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"},{"text":"Through a repeated refrain and the image of a cracked bowl, Ferreira-Hale shows that patience means accepting results one cannot fully control.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ferreira-Hale suggests that anyone who practices pottery long enough will stop making mistakes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Through a repeated refrain and the image of a cracked bowl, Ferreira-Hale shows that patience means accepting results one cannot fully control.$q$, $q$The draft analyzes the refrain, the line about the fire deciding, and the cracked bowl, all of which point to accepting what cannot be controlled. The summary choice lists the poem's contents but makes no claim to prove.$q$, 'draft', '86a82509-8375-5c02-b9c8-606fc16ffac7')
