   $q$The writer is thinking about cutting sentence 5 to shorten the draft. Why should the writer keep it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It explains why the first three stanzas all end with the same refrain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It proves that the speaker is a beginner who has never fired a kiln before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows the speaker cannot control the outcome, which links the waiting in the refrain to the acceptance shown in sentence 8.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is the only direct quotation in the draft, and a response needs at least one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows the speaker cannot control the outcome, which links the waiting in the refrain to the acceptance shown in sentence 8.$q$, $q$Without the line about the fire deciding, the draft would jump from waiting to acceptance with no evidence that the outcome is out of the potter's hands. The draft has several other quotations, so it is not the only one.$q$, 'draft', '86a82509-8375-5c02-b9c8-606fc16ffac7')
