insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('197bf5f5-144d-51d3-8119-51f176531634', 'wg11-writing-with-evidence-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Dimming the Coast$q$, $q$(1) In "Dimming the Coast," entomologist Rafael Quispe reports on an experiment in the town of Selby Point, where half of the streetlights were switched from bright white bulbs to dim amber ones. (2) Quispe argues that the change helped night-flying moths. (3) His team counted the moths circling each lamp and found an average of forty-one around white lamps but only six around amber ones. (4) Quispe explains that moths circling a lamp "are not feeding and are often exhausted by morning." (5) This means amber lights leave more moths free to spend the night among flowers instead of around bulbs.

(6) ____, Quispe checked the evening primrose along the roads, a wildflower that moths pollinate at night. (7) Plants near amber lamps produced 30 percent more seed pods than plants near white lamps. (8) ____

(9) Some residents worried that dimmer lights would make the streets less safe, but Quispe found no change in the number of traffic accidents reported during the experiment. (10) Quispe first became interested in moths as a child, when he raised caterpillars in a glass jar.$q$, 'draft')
