  ('e6f30c85-1305-5be7-b2b7-80e1c93f1aba', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence would best fill the blank in sentence 8?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The extra seed pods prove that amber light helps every kind of plant grow faster and taller.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Evening primrose is a yellow wildflower that opens in the evening and closes again by noon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Since moths pollinate this flower, the extra seed pods suggest that moths were actually visiting flowers near the amber lamps.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Plants near amber lamps produced more seed pods than plants near white lamps during the study.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Since moths pollinate this flower, the extra seed pods suggest that moths were actually visiting flowers near the amber lamps.$q$, $q$The choice beginning "Since moths pollinate this flower" explains why the seed pods matter: they show moths doing the pollinating the claim is about. The choice that says plants near amber lamps produced more seed pods only repeats sentence 7 without explaining it.$q$, 'draft', '197bf5f5-144d-51d3-8119-51f176531634')
