   $q$Why does sentence 7 support the claim more strongly than sentence 3 does?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 3 shows fewer moths at lamps, but sentence 7 shows a result in the flowers, evidence that moths were out feeding instead.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 7 uses a percentage, and percentages always count as stronger evidence than averages.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Sentence 7 includes more plants, so it proves that the moth counts in sentence 3 were wrong.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Sentence 3 comes from a different scientist, so it is less reliable than sentence 7.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 3 shows fewer moths at lamps, but sentence 7 shows a result in the flowers, evidence that moths were out feeding instead.$q$, $q$Fewer moths at amber lamps could mean many things, but more seed pods show that moths were doing useful work elsewhere, which is what "helped" means here. Both findings come from Quispe's team, so the source is not the difference.$q$, 'draft', '197bf5f5-144d-51d3-8119-51f176531634')
