   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence (6), would best support the point it makes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Professional transcribers usually charge by the page, which can make large projects costly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-other-point"},{"text":"At Dorsey County, four in ten volunteers later booked a research appointment to learn more about the families named in the registers.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The Pellam Woolen Mill was once the largest employer in the county.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Many people enjoy volunteering because it lets them meet new friends in their community.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-point-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At Dorsey County, four in ten volunteers later booked a research appointment to learn more about the families named in the registers.$q$, $q$Sentence (6) claims that volunteer projects build interest in history, and research appointments by former volunteers show that interest directly. The fact about professional fees supports a different point about cost.$q$, 'draft', 'ae69533e-3a40-5e0c-9356-b6792fac88eb')
