   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (10) as the conclusion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A calibrated sensor network would show Tilbury where riders breathe the worst air, giving the transit department a basis for targeted fixes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Air quality is a complicated subject that scientists are still studying.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Everyone should try to drive less and take the bus more often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"The city should immediately warn riders at every downtown stop that the air is unsafe.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-reasoning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A calibrated sensor network would show Tilbury where riders breathe the worst air, giving the transit department a basis for targeted fixes.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion restates the claim and its purpose of comparing stops to guide fixes. Issuing warnings contradicts sentence (7), where the writer agreed the sensors should not be used for official health warnings.$q$, 'draft', 'fd561ad4-6a2e-585c-b1ba-633844e72912')
