insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d492cdf2-cc0f-59be-b2e6-16301d408b35', 'wg12-argument-writing-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Returnable Containers at Saltmarsh Market$q$, $q$(1) Every Saturday, vendors at the Saltmarsh Farmers Market hand out roughly 1,800 disposable takeout containers, most of which end up in the overflowing bins by the parking lot. (2) The market should launch a deposit system in which customers pay two dollars for a sturdy reusable container and get the money back when they return it to a washing station. (3) The market committee sorted its trash last July and found that disposable containers made up nearly half of it by volume. (4) Similar programs have worked elsewhere. (5) At the Greyfield Night Market, a deposit program begun two years ago now recovers 92 percent of its containers each week, and the market's trash hauling bill has fallen by a third.

(6) Some vendors fear that customers will find the deposit annoying and buy less food. (7) This is a reasonable concern, since vendors depend on quick sales. (8) Greyfield vendors reported no drop in sales after the first month, and several said regulars visited more often because they came back to return containers. (9) Washing would be handled by a paid crew of local high school students, so vendors would not lose time at their stalls.

(10) Obviously anyone who is against this just likes making a mess.$q$, 'draft')
