  ('60991943-1fcc-5a7e-ab2a-417946879e37', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-capitalization-punctuation'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence about the only captain of the ferry: "The ferry's captain Lucia Ortega announced a short delay because of fog." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The ferry's captain: Lucia Ortega, announced a short delay because of fog.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-misplaced"},{"text":"The ferry's captain, Lucia Ortega, announced a short delay because of fog.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The ferry's captain, Lucia Ortega announced a short delay because of fog.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-closing-comma"},{"text":"The ferry's captain Lucia Ortega, announced a short delay because of fog.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-subject-verb"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The ferry's captain, Lucia Ortega, announced a short delay because of fog.$q$, $q$Since the ferry has only one captain, the name "Lucia Ortega" is a nonessential appositive and is set off by commas on both sides. Leaving out the closing comma leaves the appositive running into the verb.$q$, 'draft', null)
