  ('11147d98-c9d6-59d0-af4a-34973c53e84b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-capitalization-punctuation'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The bridge closure surprised no one ___ engineers had warned about the cracked supports for years." Which punctuation BEST signals that the second clause explains the first?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a comma","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"a colon","is_correct":true},{"text":"no punctuation","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"run-on-sentence"},{"text":"a semicolon","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-no-explanation-signal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a colon$q$, $q$A colon after a complete clause tells the reader that what follows explains or expands on it, which is exactly the relationship here. A semicolon would be grammatical, but it only links related clauses and does not signal that the second explains the first.$q$, 'draft', null)
