  ('92d00c22-fa27-538c-a20d-614b34af5551', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-capitalization-punctuation'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "Families gathered on the hillside to watch a once in a lifetime solar eclipse." Which revision is hyphenated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Families gathered on the hillside to watch a once-in-a-lifetime solar eclipse.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Families gathered on the hillside to watch a once-in-a-lifetime-solar eclipse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"hyphen-joins-noun"},{"text":"Families gathered on the hillside to watch a once-in-a lifetime solar eclipse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"incomplete-hyphenation"},{"text":"Families gathered on the hillside to watch a once in-a-lifetime solar eclipse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"incomplete-hyphenation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Families gathered on the hillside to watch a once-in-a-lifetime solar eclipse.$q$, $q$When a phrase of several words acts as a single adjective before a noun, every word in the phrase is linked, giving "once-in-a-lifetime." Leaving out any one hyphen breaks the phrase apart, and "solar eclipse" is the noun phrase being described, so it stays unhyphenated.$q$, 'draft', null)
