   $q$Each sentence below is about a documentary on glassblowers. Which sentence contains a punctuation error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Before the premiere, the director thanked three groups: the crew, the musicians, and the town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-correct-colon"},{"text":"The award-winning documentary followed a family of glassblowers; it took four years to film.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-correct-semicolon"},{"text":"The editor, who had worked on the film since the beginning, approved the final cut.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-nonrestrictive-commas"},{"text":"The documentary's closing scene, showed a furnace being lit at dawn.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The documentary's closing scene, showed a furnace being lit at dawn.$q$, $q$In "The documentary's closing scene, showed a furnace," a comma wrongly separates the subject "scene" from its verb "showed." The other sentences are correct: the semicolon joins two independent clauses, the colon follows a complete clause, and the commas set off a nonrestrictive clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
